---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSection from '../../components/content/article/ArticleSection.astro';
import ArticleTwoCol from '../../components/content/article/ArticleTwoCol.astro';
import ArticleLearnings from '../../components/content/article/ArticleLearnings.astro';
import SectionLabel from '../../components/ui/SectionLabel.astro';
import BasicPrintDisplay from '../../components/ui/BasicPrintDisplay.astro';
import NavRow from '../../components/ui/NavRow.astro';
import KeepExploring from '../../components/content/KeepExploring.astro';
import EditorialScrollSequence from '../../components/ui/EditorialScrollSequence.astro';
const questions = ['Should we build it?', 'Can it reach people?', 'Will anyone change their behaviour for it?', 'Does it deserve to exist?'].map(title => ({title}));
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="From a green-screen computer in Belfast to products, architecture and AI. Why Paul Kerr keeps building things — and what the work has taught him." current="about">
  <article class="about-story">
    <header class="container about-hero"><ArticleTwoCol>
      <SectionLabel slot="label" withDot>About / Paul Kerr</SectionLabel>
      <h1>I've been making things with computers since I was a kid.</h1>
      <p class="lede">The technology has changed a lot since my first green-screen computer. The part I love hasn't.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">Make something that didn't exist before. Put it in front of someone. <strong>See what happens.</strong></p>
    </ArticleTwoCol></header>

    <ArticleSection dark id="hello-world"><ArticleTwoCol>
      <SectionLabel slot="label">01 / Hello world</SectionLabel>
      <h2 class="h-2">My first program had a bug.</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">I grew up in Belfast. As a kid, I loved games and figuring out how technology worked. Around the mid-1980s, I got an Amstrad CPC 464.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">There were games to play. But there was also a BASIC programming manual. I started reading it.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">One of my first programs was essentially this:</p>
      <figure class="first-program"><figcaption class="mono-label">BASIC / A very small beginning</figcaption><pre><code>10 PRINT "PAUL KERR!"
20 GOTO 10</code></pre></figure>
      <p class="body-copy">My name repeated across the green monochrome screen. And I'd managed to get the spacing wrong, so the output ran together. I stopped it, changed it and ran it again.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">It was hardly sophisticated software. But <strong>I'd written instructions and made the machine do something that hadn't existed a few minutes earlier.</strong> Then I'd found something wrong, changed it and made it better.</p>
      <p class="lede">I was hooked.</p>
    </ArticleTwoCol>
    </ArticleSection>
    <BasicPrintDisplay />

    <ArticleSection dark id="software"><ArticleTwoCol>
      <SectionLabel slot="label">02 / Software</SectionLabel>
      <h2 class="h-2">For a long time, I focused on learning the engineering craft.</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">I gravitated towards maths, physics, science and computers, then studied Computer Science at Queen's University Belfast in the late 1990s.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">AI was part of that education. One computer-vision exercise involved classifying tanks in different environments and orientations. By today's standards, the techniques were primitive. At the time, software appearing to recognise something it hadn't seen before was astonishing.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">After university I worked as a developer in Belfast, London and later internationally, including on large enterprise systems. Large teams, slower feedback, a lot of coordination and expensive changes.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">I spent those years <strong>learning the engineering craft.</strong></p>
    </ArticleTwoCol></ArticleSection>

    <ArticleSection id="product"><ArticleTwoCol>
      <SectionLabel slot="label">03 / Product</SectionLabel>
      <h2 class="h-2">Then I became interested in everything around the code.</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">Moneytech was an important early experience. I joined while the company and product were still being established. The work wasn't neatly divided into engineering, product and operations. We did what was needed.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">We built software, dealt with security, worked on the user experience and handled operational jobs that would never appear in a developer job description.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">It was one of the first times I really understood that <strong>software doesn't exist by itself.</strong> It sits inside a product. The product sits inside a business. And eventually somebody has to use the thing.</p>
    </ArticleTwoCol></ArticleSection>

    <ArticleSection dark id="the-interface"><ArticleTwoCol>
      <SectionLabel slot="label">04 / The interface</SectionLabel>
      <h2 class="h-2">The part I kept coming back to was the person on the other side.</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">I enjoyed programming itself. Well-structured code could feel elegant. But the strongest reward was watching someone actually use something I'd helped create.</p>
      <p class="body-copy"><strong>I loved the moment when something stopped being code and became an experience.</strong> Someone clicked it. Touched it. Walked through a door because of it. Put on a headset. Asked it a question.</p>
      <p class="lede">And occasionally said: that's cool.</p>
    </ArticleTwoCol>
      <div class="experience-montage">
        <figure><a href="/shipped/amica/" aria-label="Read the Amica story"><img src="/media/work/amica/lobby.webp" width="1440" height="900" alt="People moving through the International Towers lobby, alongside digital community screens" loading="lazy" /></a><figcaption>Use a place. / Amica</figcaption></figure>
        <figure><a href="/shipped/boxofficevr/" aria-label="Read the BoxOfficeVR story"><img src="/media/work/boxofficevr/mobile-viewer.webp" width="1437" height="681" alt="A theatre performance playing on a phone in a VR viewer" loading="lazy" /></a><figcaption>Enter a performance. / BoxOfficeVR</figcaption></figure>
      </div>
    </ArticleSection>

    <ArticleSection id="whole-system"><ArticleTwoCol>
      <SectionLabel slot="label">05 / The whole system</SectionLabel>
      <h2 class="h-2">Eventually I stopped thinking about the screen in isolation.</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">The work expanded from frontend to backend and cloud, then into architecture, operations, physical systems and teams. I was increasingly working where business problems, product decisions and technical architecture met.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">That became my work as a CTO and product architect. <strong>Architecture, to me, isn't drawing boxes around technology.</strong> It's understanding enough of the system to make good decisions about what should exist, how the pieces fit together and what happens when real people start using it.</p>
    </ArticleTwoCol></ArticleSection>

    <ArticleSection dark id="judgement"><ArticleTwoCol>
      <SectionLabel slot="label">06 / Judgement</SectionLabel>
      <h2 class="h-2">Building it turned out to be only part of the job.</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">Craveable showed me what happens when product, technology, operations and distribution line up at scale. Neurotechnology showed me that technology could work while reaching people remained difficult. BoxOfficeVR showed me that people could love an experience without changing their behaviour.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">Earlier in my career, the question was usually <strong>can we build it?</strong> The questions got harder:</p>
      <div class="dark-primitives"><ArticleLearnings items={questions} /></div>
      <p class="body-copy">I still love difficult engineering. I've just learned that <strong>solving the engineering problem doesn't automatically solve the product.</strong></p>
    </ArticleTwoCol></ArticleSection>

    <ArticleSection id="new-again"><ArticleTwoCol>
      <SectionLabel slot="label">07 / New again</SectionLabel>
      <h2 class="h-2">Then software started feeling new again.</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">After decades of building software, some kinds of work had become familiar. Websites. Content systems. Business applications. Cloud platforms.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">I'd studied AI at university and spent years watching it progress mostly at the edges of everyday software. Then suddenly <strong>things that once felt like research problems became things I could build with.</strong></p>
      <p class="body-copy">Software could see, listen and speak. It could reason across information, help write the software itself and participate in an interface rather than simply wait for a button click.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">I didn't expect some of this to become practical in my working lifetime. Then it happened very quickly.</p>
      <p class="lede">It brought back a feeling I recognised.</p>
    </ArticleTwoCol></ArticleSection>

    <ArticleSection dark id="now"><ArticleTwoCol>
      <SectionLabel slot="label">08 / Now</SectionLabel>
      <h2 class="h-2">So I'm building again.</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">AI-assisted development has changed the scale at which I can work personally. Ideas that once required a team just to test can now become working software quickly enough to learn from.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">That's brought me surprisingly close to where I started: <strong>having an idea, building it, putting it in front of someone and seeing what happens.</strong></p>
      <div class="dark-primitives current-links">
        <NavRow href="/building/" label="Building" description="Kerrzo and Brilliancy. Two ideas I'm taking beyond the experiment." />
        <NavRow href="/experiments/" label="Experimenting" description="Poszo, Wi-Fi human sensing and AI podcast production. Questions I'm testing." />
        <NavRow href="/learnings/" label="Writing" description="The things the work is teaching me, while they're still fresh." />
      </div>
    </ArticleTwoCol></ArticleSection>

    <ArticleSection id="away"><ArticleTwoCol>
      <SectionLabel slot="label">09 / Away from the screen</SectionLabel>
      <h2 class="h-2">Away from the screen.</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">I'm still a fairly unapologetic geek. I play chess, play games, read science fiction and fantasy, and spend an unreasonable amount of time wondering whether some new piece of technology can be turned into something useful.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">I also like running and getting outside. And building things even when nobody has asked me to.</p>
      <p class="body-copy"><strong>Sydney has been home for most of my adult life.</strong> It's where I live with my family.</p>
    </ArticleTwoCol></ArticleSection>

    <ArticleSection dark id="same-experiment"><ArticleTwoCol>
      <SectionLabel slot="label">10 / Still the same experiment</SectionLabel>
      <h2 class="h-2">Still the same experiment.</h2>
      <p class="body-copy">The Amstrad is long gone. The machines are faster. The interfaces are better. And what one person can build has changed beyond recognition.</p>
      <p class="body-copy">But the thing I enjoy is basically the same.</p>
    </ArticleTwoCol></ArticleSection>

    <EditorialScrollSequence
      tone="light"
      size="large"
      lines={[
        "Make something that wasn't there.",
        'Put it in front of someone.',
        'See what happens.',
      ]}
    />
  </article>
  <KeepExploring routes={['building','shipped','experiments']} descriptions={{building:"See what I'm working on now.",shipped:"See the products and systems I've helped deliver.",experiments:"See the questions I'm testing."}} />
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .about-hero { padding-top: clamp(140px,19vh,200px); padding-bottom: clamp(64px,10vh,120px); }
  h1 { font-size: clamp(38px,5.5vw,82px); line-height: 1.04; letter-spacing: -.04em; max-width: 21ch; text-wrap: balance; }
  .first-program { margin: 40px 0 0; border-block: 1px solid var(--color-dark-border); padding-block: clamp(24px,4vw,48px); }
  .first-program pre { margin: 24px 0 0; font: clamp(16px,2.6vw,34px)/1.7 var(--font-mono); white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; color: var(--color-dark-fg); }
  .first-program code { font: inherit; }

  .experience-montage { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0,1.2fr) minmax(0,.8fr); gap: clamp(24px,4vw,64px); align-items: end; margin-top: 48px; }
  .experience-montage figure { margin: 0; min-width: 0; }
  .experience-montage img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; border-radius: var(--radius-md); }
  .experience-montage figcaption { color: var(--color-dark-body); font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; margin-top: 16px; }
  .dark-primitives { --color-ink:var(--color-dark-fg); --color-body:var(--color-dark-body); --color-label:var(--color-dark-label); --color-border:var(--color-dark-border); }
  .current-links { border-top: 1px solid var(--color-dark-border); }
  @media(max-width:640px) { .experience-montage { grid-template-columns:1fr; gap:36px; } }
</style>

